<title>FRANCE: France seeks adviser bank for state share sales.</title>
<headline>France seeks adviser bank for state share sales.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French government launched a tender last week to appoint a bank adviser on the sale of shares in its minority holdings, business daily l'Agefi said on Monday.</p>
<p>Its Elf Aquitaine and Renault stakes are not among the stakes to be sold, the report said.</p>
<p>At least 10 banks were said to have been contacted since the tender opened on September 17 and meetings are expected to be held in the next few days, it said. The holdings being sold include shares in Pechiney, Usinor Sacilor, Credit Local de France, Seita and Roussel-Uclaf.</p>
<p>Other stakes include Rhone-Poulenc, Union des Assurances de Paris, Banque Nationale de Paris, and Assurances Generales de France, the newspaper reported.</p>
<p>The value of these holdings is estimated at between eight and 10 billion francs, the report said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452.</p>
